/target
Cargo.lock
prds/site/

# Generated cargo-tarpaulin report artifacts (`just coverage`)
/tarpaulin-report.*
/cobertura.xml
/XmlCobertura.xml
/lcov.info

# LOCAL SANDBOX (scripts/sandbox-build.sh) - never commit.
# The sandbox itself now lives outside the repo (../.xaft-agtrs-sandbox/); this
# entry is kept so an older in-tree sandbox can never be committed either.
.agtrs-sandbox/

# LOCAL PORT VERIFICATION (scripts/verify-agtrs-port.sh) - never commit.
# Unlike the sandbox above, that script clones agtrs into a scratch directory
# INSIDE the repo and removes it only from an EXIT/INT/TERM trap, so a SIGKILL
# during its cargo check can leave a whole clone sitting here. Ignored so that
# `git add -A` from a dirty tree cannot commit it either. Deliberately written
# without the trailing slash `.agtrs-sandbox/` uses: git only matches a
# trailing-slash pattern against a directory that EXISTS, so that form answers
# `git check-ignore .tmp-agtrs-check` with nothing on a clean checkout.
.tmp-agtrs-check

# Python bytecode from scripts/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.agenthicc/
tests/.cassette/
